Below is a simple PHP-based contact form handler that processes user input and stores it in a file. It includes:
- Input sanitization
- Prevention of XSS
- Safe storage (plain text log)

---

### ✅ Example: Secure Contact Form Handler (PHP)

#### 1. HTML Form (`contact.html`)
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <title>Contact Us</title>
</head>
<body>
  <h2>Contact Form</h2>
  <form action="process_contact.php" method="POST">
    <label>Name: <input type="text" name="name" required></label><br><br>
    <label>Email: <input type="email" name="email" required></label><br><br>
    <label>Message: <textarea name="message" required></textarea></label><br><br>
    <button type="submit">Send</button>
  </form>
</body>
</html>
```

#### 2. PHP Processor (`process_contact.php`)
```php
<?php
// Define the file to store submissions
$logFile = 'submissions.log';

// Sanitize and validate inputs
$name = filter_input(INPUT_POST, 'name', FILTER_SANITIZE_STRING);
$email = filter_input(INPUT_POST, 'email', FILTER_VALIDATE_EMAIL);
$message = filter_input(INPUT_POST, 'message', FILTER_SANITIZE_STRING);

// Basic validation
if (!$name || !$email || !$message) {
    die("Invalid input detected.");
}

// Escape for safe logging (prevent log injection)
$entry = sprintf(
    "[%s] Name: %s | Email: %s | Message: %s\n",
    date('Y-m-d H:i:s'),
    htmlspecialchars($name, ENT_QUOTES, 'UTF-8'),
    htmlspecialchars($email, ENT_QUOTES, 'UTF-8'),
    htmlspecialchars($message, ENT_QUOTES, 'UTF-8')
);

// Append to log file
if (file_put_contents($logFile, $entry, FILE_APPEND | LOCK_EX)) {
    echo "Thank you, $name! Your message has been sent.";
} else {
    echo "Failed to save your message. Please try again later.";
}
?>
```

---

### 🔐 Security Notes:
- **`FILTER_SANITIZE_STRING`** (deprecated in PHP 8.1+) — for older versions, it removes tags. In newer PHP, consider `htmlspecialchars()` or manual sanitization.
- **`FILTER_VALIDATE_EMAIL`** ensures the email is at least syntactically valid.
- **`htmlspecialchars()`** prevents XSS when displaying logs.
- **`FILE_APPEND | LOCK_EX`** ensures thread-safe writing.

> ⚠️ For production, use a database with prepared statements (e.g., PDO), CSRF protection, rate limiting, and proper authentication.

